{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1499233-characters-that-have-visited-the-labyrinth","id":1499233,"title":"Characters That Have Visited The Labyrinth?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-09T12:29:11-08:00","id":1499233,"title":"Characters That Have Visited The Labyrinth?","content":"Does anyone know of any non wraith canon characters (vampires, mages, etc) that have visited the underworld Labyrinth and come back, or at least characters you feel are capable of doing so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T11:22:36-08:00","id":1499297,"title":"","content":"The best canon example that I can think of is <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Xerxes_Jones?so=search\" target=\"_blank\">Xerxes Jones</a>. Admittedly, he did not make it back, but that seems to have more to do with the specific VERY BAD IDEA he was involved with rather than a fundamental limit on his ability to return; it seems like the Void Engineers are capable of producing vessels capable of traversing the Labyrinth with relative safety. Based on that, I would assume that it would be at least hypothetically possible for others to do so, though I'd imagine the necessary protection would be considerable.<br /> <br /> Thought that just popped into my head as writing this: was Xerxes being able to get that close to Oblivion an elaborate case of &quot;just as planned&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T20:22:12-08:00","id":1499346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1499233-characters-that-have-visited-the-labyrinth?p=1499297#post1499297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best canon example that I can think of is <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Xerxes_Jones?so=search\" target=\"_blank\">Xerxes Jones</a>. Admittedly, he did not make it back, but that seems to have more to do with the specific VERY BAD IDEA he was involved with rather than a fundamental limit on his ability to return; it seems like the Void Engineers are capable of producing vessels capable of traversing the Labyrinth with relative safety. Based on that, I would assume that it would be at least hypothetically possible for others to do so, though I'd imagine the necessary protection would be considerable.<br /> <br /> Thought that just popped into my head as writing this: was Xerxes being able to get that close to Oblivion an elaborate case of &quot;just as planned&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the first Relic Nuke being used on Enoch which triggered the premature detonation of Jones' nuke was set up by Ferrymen at the behest of Anubis over an old debt they owed him, I'd say there's a good chance that's the case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T21:39:29-08:00","id":1499347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1499233-characters-that-have-visited-the-labyrinth?p=1499346#post1499346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the first Relic Nuke being used on Enoch which triggered the premature detonation of Jones' nuke was set up by Ferrymen at the behest of Anubis over an old debt they owed him, I'd say there's a good chance that's the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I was aware, blowing up Enoch was the entire point of that favor, but I haven't dug deeply into Wraith material. That's quite a potential rabbit-hole!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T08:07:53-08:00","id":1499649,"title":"","content":"Too bad we never found out what Anubis even was. A wraith? An Incarna? A Plasmic? We\u2019ll never know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T18:33:55-08:00","id":1499707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1499233-characters-that-have-visited-the-labyrinth?p=1499649#post1499649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too bad we never found out what Anubis even was. A wraith? An Incarna? A Plasmic? We\u2019ll never know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish we had more things like this in WoD. I have always being glad about that kind of thing in Wraith. But then the authors have to ruin everything by suggesting that the Lady of Fate might be Eve...<br /> <br /> That's one of the things I love about the world of Tolkien. What is the nature of Ungoliant? Or Tom Bombadill? Or the nameless things under Moria? Nobody knows. And when I say nobody, IT REALLY MEANS IT. And that's freaking great.<br /> <br /> I wish that were the case for Vampires in WoD too. I wish there werent a single line written about the fabled third generation. Not even a single name about them. Who are them? What are them? Nobody knows. They are probably 13 (hence why 13 &quot;clans&quot;), but no one can tell for sure, just a huge mystery. It would be so much better.<br /> <br /> So, we have Anubis. What the hell he even is? Nobody knows. And that's great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T07:38:33-08:00","id":1500035,"title":"","content":"To be fair, they only confirmed that the Lady was Eve in <i>Ends of Empire</i>, the end of WtO. And while it's successor Orpheus brought Abel around in <i>End Game</i> they made it very clear that not even he is entirely sure what he is or even if he name from when he was alive was Abel. In fact he even says he might actually be the embodiment of murder victims rather than an actual wraith.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of Grandmother in Orpheus and how multiple ideas of what she is thrown out but with no clear idea if any of them are right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T01:32:57-08:00","id":1500274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1499233-characters-that-have-visited-the-labyrinth?p=1499707#post1499707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish we had more things like this in WoD. I have always being glad about that kind of thing in Wraith. But then the authors have to ruin everything by suggesting that the Lady of Fate might be Eve...<br /> <br /> That's one of the things I love about the world of Tolkien. What is the nature of Ungoliant? Or Tom Bombadill? Or the nameless things under Moria? Nobody knows. And when I say nobody, IT REALLY MEANS IT. And that's freaking great.<br /> <br /> I wish that were the case for Vampires in WoD too. I wish there werent a single line written about the fabled third generation. Not even a single name about them. Who are them? What are them? Nobody knows. They are probably 13 (hence why 13 &amp;quot;clans&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but no one can tell for sure, just a huge mystery. It would be so much better.<br /> <br /> So, we have Anubis. What the hell he even is? Nobody knows. And that's great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to solutions for this:<br /> 1. Ignore canon. Take what you want and remove what you dislike. This is a great solution for a storyteller.<br /> 2. Play Chronicles of Darkness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T13:21:37-08:00","id":1500328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1499233-characters-that-have-visited-the-labyrinth#post1499233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know of any non wraith canon characters (vampires, mages, etc) that have visited the underworld Labyrinth and come back, or at least characters you feel are capable of doing so?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Harbingers of Skulls, ie Cappadocians who went to Enoch. Depending on how you want to interpret it, all Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> Some Eonchians actually explored the Labyrinth. A 4th gen Tzimi (Andeleon) and a Lich (Yamadanda) are mentioned.<br /> <br /> I guess anything of abyssal nature would have a bit of 'home advantage' in making it through. Since the different game lines are vague and/or contradictory about that part, that may include Demons, Baali, Lasombra, Nagaraja, banes, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T04:00:15-08:00","id":1501797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1499233-characters-that-have-visited-the-labyrinth#post1499233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know of any non wraith canon characters (vampires, mages, etc) that have visited the underworld Labyrinth and come back, or at least characters you feel are capable of doing so?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Mage perspective, Nephandi could visit the Labyrinth, even the Euthanatoi (Voormas could be that kind of character). From Werewolf, the Silent Striders and Black Spiral Dancers are the more akin to the underworld, in some Wraith books (Haunter guildbook) is even stated that the Labyrinth is the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}